  "content": {
    "component": "news_article",
    "_uid": "2667-root",
    "title": "Trade, Heritage and Landscape along the Silk Roads",
    "subtitle": null,
    "summary": "Part of a Series of Talks Supporting 'The Silk Road: A Living History'  Exhibition",
    "media": [
      {
        "_uid": "d2ee8d00b66b53c4",
        "component": "news_media",
        "role": "banner",
        "filename": "2667-BannerImage.jpg",
        "src": "/news-media/2667-BannerImage.jpg",
        "media_type": "image",
        "caption": null,
        "alt": "Trade, Heritage and Landscape along the Silk Roads"
      }
    ],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "During this \n      "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "webinar",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "https://youtu.be/Vkab7Ic_QaA",
                    "target": "_blank",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " chaired by Professor Stéphane Pradines; Professor Roland Lin and Professor Michael Jansen discuss the Silk Roads and networks between Asia, Africa and Europe. The experts focus particularly on the land and maritime routes in Central Asia and the Indian Ocean. With some historical and archaeological examples, the discussants will show how Emporiums, city-States and thalassocracies were created around commercial networks."
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n      "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "'The Silk Road: A Living History' ",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "https://silkroad-livinghistory.org/",
                    "target": "_blank",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "talks are a collaboration between The Aga Khan Foundation, UK, The Institute of Ismaili Studies and the Aga Khan University's Institute for the Study of Muslim Civilisations."
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
